content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "DE bearing housing vibration is 7.6 mm/s. The limit is Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual, which classifies the highest bearing-housing reading. 7.6 mm/s is above the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary, so it falls in Zone D (red): 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The pump must be stopped.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "DE bearing housing temperature is 84 C, measured on the housing surface. The manual limits are: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is 4 C above the alarm limit and 6 C below the trip limit, so it is in the alarm band. Under 5.3 this counts as 'high temperature'.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Water is dripping from the shaft area at about 1 drop/s. The troubleshooting table lists this as 'Leakage at shaft seal'. No allowable leakage rate is documented, so the drip is treated as a seal fault.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pump ran dry for about 10 minutes during a tank changeover. This breaches the specification for Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge: 'never run dry'.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal faces damaged by the dry run, causing the shaft seal leak. 'Seal run dry' is a listed cause of seal leakage. The fitted seal type is unknown (see open_questions). If it is the component seal HF3-450, note that SB-2026-014 reports early failures of HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000, which also applies to this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "DE bearing wear or damage. This would explain both the Zone D vibration and the alarm-level temperature. Bearing wear is a listed cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is a listed cause common to all three symptoms: seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation. These are listed causes of high vibration and should be checked while the assembly is out.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. This is a listed cause of high bearing temperature only.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 now (vibration is in Zone D). Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before stripping, record the vibration on both bearing housings (DE and NDE) and the bearing temperatures as a baseline. Check the grease quantity in the bearings.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller and wear rings for damage or imbalance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm. No sleeve setting measurement is needed for the HF3-450B cartridge seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: DE bearing 6312-C3 (HF3-512) and NDE bearing 6310-C3 (HF3-510). The DE bearing shows high temperature and Zone D vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450 on this serial. Tighten the M10 seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, per SB-2026-014, not the 25 Nm in Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Refit the impeller and tighten the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the M12 bearing housing bolts to 85 Nm, lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120. Refit the back pull-out assembly and tighten the M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the pump and motor, since the work disturbs the bearing housing. Tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in place. Prime and fill the pump before start so it never runs dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings. Confirm it is in Zone A/B (no more than 4.5 mm/s RMS, and not in Zone C) and that housing temperature stays at or below 70 C. Confirm there is no seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set. Supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Replaced as a pair with the DE bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Have one available; fit only if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately: Zone D means 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. Do not restart until repairs are complete.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Ensure the casing is full and the Plan 11 seal flush is working before start-up, and prevent a repeat dry run at tank changeover.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing is at 84 C (alarm level). Allow it to cool before handling.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians (standard time).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians (standard time).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician (standard time).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Plan up to 11.5 h if the standard times are simply added: 10.0 h for 2 technicians plus 1.5 h for 1 technician. The actual time may be lower because both jobs share the same disassembly (see open_questions).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number. The manual parts list (C05) gives HF3-450 component seal. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (14 March 2026) says do NOT fit HF3-450 on HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above; use HF3-450B. Serial HF3-22871 is in the bulletin's range, so the bulletin applies: fit HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque. Manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm. SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B and states that only pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use Table 5. Use 30 Nm for this serial. All other Table 5 torques are not changed by the bulletin and still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling. Manual 5.2 says inspect the sleeve for scoring. The bulletin says no sleeve measurement is needed for pre-set HF3-450B, but to replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. Apply the bulletin: no setting measurement, but inspect scoring depth against the 0.1 mm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal is currently fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? This is not in the evidence and affects root-cause analysis.",
    "Is the reported 7.6 mm/s an RMS value, as Figure 3 requires? What is the NDE bearing housing reading?",
    "The manual gives no allowable seal leakage rate.",
    "The manual gives no grease type, quantity or interval to check against over-greasing.",
    "There is no labour time for fitting the HF3-450B cartridge seal. How much do the seal and bearing jobs overlap, given they share disassembly?",
    "Is a replacement impeller (HF3-210) needed? It depends on inspection, and no acceptance limits for impeller or wear-ring wear are given.",
    "The evidence covers no lockout/isolation procedure details, no NPSH data for a cavitation check, and no bearing fitting method.",
    "The evidence does not explain how the dry run at tank changeover should be prevented (e.g. low-level interlock)."
  ]
}
